                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cdots
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#MaximalCompactSubalgebra Maximal compact subalgebra
          %p
            In contrast to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔢
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 10
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{e}_{10(10)}
            itself, its “
            %a{:href => "Kac-Moody+algebra#OnMaximalCompactSubalgebra"}> maximal compact subalgebra
            ”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔨
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 10
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{k}_{10(10)}
            has non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+representation"} trivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+space"} finite dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
            (
            %a{:href => "#KleinschmidtNicolaiVigano20"}> Kleinschmidt, Nicolai &amp; Vigano 2020
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "Kac-Moody+algebra#KKLN22"} KKLN22
          %p
            Among these is in particular a spinor representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 32
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{32}
            and a vector-spinor representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 320
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{320}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 32
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 320
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Rep
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi fdim
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔨
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 10
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{32}
                  ,\,
                  \\mathbf{320}
                  \\;\in\;
                  Rep^{fdim}_{\mathbb{R}}\big(\mathfrak{k}_{10(10)}\big)
          %p
            akin to the familiar reps of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 10
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{so}(10)
            of the same name/dimension &amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#deBuylHenneauxPaulot05"}> deBuyl, Henneaux &amp; Paulot 2005 §8
            ,
            = succeed "&rbrack;." do
              %a{:href => "#KleinschmidtNicolai06"} Kleinschmidt &amp; Nicolai 2006
          %p
            Remarkably, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+algebra"} symmetrized
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+representations"} tensor product
            of this spinorial
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 32
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{32}
            with itself decomposes as a 1-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+representation"} trivial representation
            with a 527-dimensional
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irrep"} irrep
